    "title": "CONFIRMED lineups: Real Madrid vs Atlético de Madrid, 2026 La Liga - Yahoo Sports",
    "text": "AdvertisementAdvertisementAdvertisementAdvertisementTRENDINGYankees shut out GiantsJudge's golden sombreroSign up for fantasy baseballOpening day starting pitchersSweet 16 previewStory byLucas NavarreteSun, March 22, 2026 at 6:27 PM UTC·1 min readAdd Yahoo Sports on GoogleReal Madrid have published their starting lineup for the upcoming match against Atlético de Madrid in La Liga. Los Blancos need the three points to keep the race for the 2025-26 Liga title competitive, as Barcelona got the win at home against Rayo Vallecano.STARTING LINEUPS:Real Madrid starting XI: Lunin, Carvajal, Rudiger, Huijsen, Fran, Tchouameni, Valverde, Thiago, Güler, Vinicius, Brahim.AdvertisementAdvertisementAdvertisementAtlético de Madrid starting XI (TBC): Musso; Molina, Giménez, Hancko, Ruggeri; Giuliano, Llorente, Cardoso, Baena; Julián, Sorloth.HOW TO WATCH, STREAM LA LIGADate: 03/22/2026Time: 21:00 CET, 03:00pm EST.Venue: Santiago Bernabeu, Madrid, Spain.Available TV: DAZN La Liga (Spain), ESPN Deportes (USA).Available Streaming: ESPN+ (USA)Managing Madrid has affiliate partnerships. These do not influence editorial content, though Vox Media may earn commissions for products purchased via affiliate links.AdvertisementAdvertisementTerms and Privacy PolicyYour Privacy ChoicesAbout Our AdsAdvertisementAdvertisementAdvertisementStory byMANCHESTER, ENGLAND - MARCH 17: Real Madrid head coach Alvaro Arbeloa applauds the fans at the final whistle of the UEFA Champions League 2025/26 Round of 16 Second Leg match between Manchester City FC and Real Madrid CF at City of Manchester Stadium on March 17, 2026 in Manchester, United Kingdom. (Photo by Alex Dodd - CameraSport via Getty Images) | CameraSport via Getty ImagesineednonameTue, March 24, 2026 at 8:30 PM UTC·1 min readAs two of national teams across the world gear up for final preparations before the World Cup, Real Madrid coach Álvaro Arbeloa contemplates the starting lineup he’ll use against Bayern Munich next month. Two names stand out from the crowd: Kylian Mbappe and Jude Bellingham.Bellingham and Mbappe have spent most of the season unfit and injured, but they have recently returned to the pitch. They were both called up to their respective national teams and are likely to feature in some capacity. According to Defensa Central, Arbeloa is planning to have both these players in the starting XI versus Bayern Munich — assuming they are actually fit.AdvertisementAdvertisementAdvertisementWhy risk it?Aoccrding to the report, Arbeloa’s performance in the Champions League will determine his future at the club. Currently, he has the backing of the squad, something Xabi Alonso never achieved. However, for the Spaniard to remain in charge beyond this season, he will need to impress Florentino Perez, which is a whole different ball game.The game against FC Bayern, therefore, is existential for the coach. He will put his best players on the pitch if he can, which means getting Bellingham and Mbappe in the starting lineup. As for Kompany, nothing changes in his planning. Whether Mbappe and Bellingham play or not, the Bavarians will prepare the same way they always have.AdvertisementAdvertisementAbout Our AdsAdvertisementAdvertisementAdvertisement",
